  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="content-area" style="max-width: 850px;">
        
        <header class="article-header">
          <span class="article-category">Technology</span>
          <h1 class="article-title">Revolutionary Oil-Filtration Technology Debuts in Latest Range Hood Models</h1>
          <div class="article-meta-info">
            <span>📅 October 2024</span>
            <span>🏷️ Technology</span>
            <span>⏱️ 6 min read</span>
          </div>
        </header>

        <figure class="article-image-figure">
          <div style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/9;background:linear-gradient(135deg, #7c3aed, #5b21b6);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border-radius:var(--radius-lg);">
            <svg width="120" height="120" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.3)" stroke-width="1">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/>
              <path d="M12 1v4M12 19v4M4.22 4.22l2.83 2.83M16.95 16.95l2.83 2.83M1 12h4M19 12h4M4.22 19.78l2.83-2.83M16.95 7.05l2.83-2.83"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="article-image-caption">HouseTech's advanced oil-filtration technology</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="article-body">
          <p>Shenzhen, China — HouseTech Group announces the launch of its proprietary CycloClean oil-filtration system, a groundbreaking technology that achieves 99.8% grease separation efficiency—significantly outperforming industry standards. This innovation represents HouseTech's ongoing commitment to developing advanced kitchen ventilation solutions for OEM partners worldwide.</p>
          
          <p>Traditional range hood filters typically achieve 70-85% grease separation efficiency, with the remaining grease particles entering the exhaust system and potentially causing fire hazards or environmental concerns. HouseTech's engineering team spent three years developing the CycloClean system to address these challenges.</p>
          
          <h2>How CycloClean Works</h2>
          <p>The CycloClean system combines multiple filtration stages in a single, elegantly designed unit:</p>
          
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Centrifugal Pre-separator:</strong> Large grease particles are forced to the outer walls through high-speed rotation before reaching the main filter.</li>
            <li><strong>Electrostatic Main Filter:</strong> Charged filter plates attract and capture micro-particles invisible to the naked eye.</li>
            <li><strong>Activated Carbon Final Stage:</strong> Eliminates odors and ensures clean air exhaust for recirculating models.</li>
            <li><strong>Self-Draining Design:</strong> Collected grease automatically flows to a collection reservoir for easy disposal.</li>
          </ul>

          <blockquote>
            "The CycloClean system represents a paradigm shift in range hood filtration. Our OEM partners can now offer products that not only perform better but also reduce maintenance requirements and environmental impact. This aligns with HouseTech's vision of sustainable manufacturing."
            <cite>— HouseTech Chief Technology Officer</cite>
          </blockquote>

          <h2>Environmental and Economic Benefits</h2>
          <p>Beyond superior performance, CycloClean offers significant advantages for end-users and the environment:</p>
          
          <p>Unlike disposable aluminum filters that end up in landfills, HouseTech's CycloClean filters are completely washable and dishwasher-safe. This eliminates ongoing filter replacement costs for consumers and reduces environmental waste. The system also extends the life of exhaust ducts by preventing grease buildup, reducing fire risks and maintenance costs for commercial kitchens.</p>

          <h2>Availability for OEM Partners</h2>
          <p>HouseTech's CycloClean technology is now available for integration into OEM product lines. The technology can be adapted to fit various range hood form factors and designs, giving HouseTech's manufacturing clients a competitive advantage in their markets. Customization options include filter geometry, collection reservoir capacity, and integration with smart home systems for filter maintenance alerts.</p>
          
          <p>For B2B inquiries about CycloClean technology integration or private-label opportunities, HouseTech's engineering team welcomes discussions with interested OEM partners and brand distributors.</p>
        </div>

